// ===========================================================================
// games/sonic4/data/sound/dac_banks.emp — the DAC sample banks, native (K4 inc-5
// Stage 2, the P2 probe)
// ===========================================================================
// The ROM-streamed DAC sample banks were the flat BINCLUDE island in
// games/sonic4/main.asm's gameSoundDataIncludes. This module places them
// NATIVELY by EMBEDDING the seam-2-emitted artifacts (dac_blip_bank.bin /
// dac_shared_bank.bin) at their bank-aligned LMAs — the P2 path (spec §6): the
// emit-tool architecture is untouched (`ensure_generated` still lowers
// dac_samples.emp → the .bin; this module just places those bytes natively
// instead of via AS BINCLUDE). The .bin are gitignored build artifacts, so the
// golden gate (dac_bank_port) runs `ensure_generated` first (emit-first).
//
// The two banks live one $8000 window apart so a single Z80 bank id covers each
// and FILL never re-banks mid-sample: the blip bank sits at the `dac_banks` map
// anchor and the shared drum bank one 0x8000 window above it. Both are declared map
// anchors (when="sound_on"). What is FIXED about them is the 0x8000 alignment — one
// Z80 `SetBank` window — and their order; the LMAs themselves are DERIVED from the
// packed-data end by the bank placement rule, so they move when the data grows. The
// `align $8000` between the two banks is the inter-bank pad (the intervening bytes
// are $00 fill, matching the reference). One section, one head label Dac_Temp_Blip
// (the section head + the map-order/frozen boundary key) — the shared-bank labels
// are mid-section.
//
// ⚠ THE ADDRESSES AND BANK IDS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT WRITTEN HERE (2026-08-27). This
// header carried `$48000`/`$50000` and banks `$9`/`$A` until the 2026-08-26 re-layout
// moved them, and it kept saying so afterwards because NOTHING EXECUTES A HEADER
// COMMENT — no gate could contradict it. Re-typing today's values would go stale on
// the identical clock. The live derivation lives in `games/sonic4/map.toml` (search
// `dac_banks  = align_up`), which records both the rule and the measured result; the
// `.lst` is the instrument for where they actually landed.
// Found by the sigil lane during the SIGIL-DECOUPLE constraint audit, and it survived
// this repo's own prose sweep because it describes addresses the re-layout parcel
// MOVED rather than addresses that parcel TOUCHED.
//
// STRUCTURAL EXCLUSIVITY (spec §6, the ruled mechanism): this native section is
// the SOLE DAC placement — the AS BINCLUDE arm is DELETED, so it can't double-
// place (can't-both); it is unconditionally in the sound-on registry, so it can't
// go missing (can't-neither). The map anchor validation + the whole-ROM byte gate
// enforce it loudly.
//
// The SND_* per-sample {bank,ptr,len} triples are NOT here — they are folded into
// the DacSampleTable head (dac_sample_tab.bin) at emit from dac_samples.emp's
// bankid()/winptr() equs, so the main build's Dac_* labels have no runtime
// consumer; they are placement heads only.
// ===========================================================================

module games.sonic4.dac_banks in dac_banks

const _blip   = embed("engine/sound/generated/dac_blip_bank.bin")
const _shared = embed("engine/sound/generated/dac_shared_bank.bin")

// The blip bring-up sample — alone in its own 0x8000 window at the `dac_banks` anchor.
pub data Dac_Temp_Blip = _blip

// Pad to the next 0x8000 bank boundary: the shared drum bank starts on
// its own bank id — one window above the blip bank's, whatever the rule placed
// that at — so FILL never re-banks mid-sample. (`bankid()` folds the id at link
// from the placed LMA; nothing here is hand-typed. See the ⚠ note in the header.)
align $8000

// The shared RAW 8-bit PCM drum bank, one 0x8000 window above the anchor. Dac_SharedBank_Start and
// Dac_Kick coincide at the bank head (the first drum is the kick).
pub data Dac_SharedBank_Start = Data.empty
pub data Dac_Kick = _shared
